# mariadb-server.cnf (replaces /etc/my.cnf.d/mariadb-server.cnf)   READ: docs/08
#
# PURPOSE
#   Alpine's default config has `skip-networking`, so MariaDB only listens on its
#   unix socket and WordPress (another container) can't connect. This file fixes that.
#
# WRITE under a [mariadbd] (or [mysqld]) group:
#   skip-networking = 0       (or simply don't set skip-networking)
#   bind-address    = 0.0.0.0 (listen on the container's interface)
#   port            = 3306
#   datadir         = /var/lib/mysql   (← the named volume)
#   socket          = /run/mysqld/mysqld.sock
#   character-set-server = utf8mb4 / collation-server = utf8mb4_unicode_ci
#   (optional) innodb_buffer_pool_size, sized for your VM's RAM
#
# CHECK
#   docker exec mariadb mariadb-admin -u root -p variables | grep -E "skip_networking|bind"
